          "id": "GENUS_TACHYBAPTUS",
          "name": "Tachybaptus",
          "rank": "GENUS",
          "description": "Little grebes — the smallest and most compact of all grebes, found on a much wider range of water bodies than their larger relatives. The little grebe (smådopping) is a remarkably buoyant bird, riding high on the water like a cork and diving suddenly with a smooth, almost silent plunge. Despite its tiny size it is feisty and territorial, driving away intruders many times its own size with a loud, shrill whinny. Little grebes are one of the most widespread wetland birds in Sweden, found on ponds as small as a few hundred square metres — anywhere there is aquatic vegetation for nesting and small fish or invertebrates to eat. In autumn they can aggregate in small flocks on larger lakes before moving to coastal wintering areas.",
          "lineage": "Small Grebes",
